<title>ITALY: ALPINE SKIING-PROFILE OF MEN'S DOWNHILL WINNER.</title>
<headline>ALPINE SKIING-PROFILE OF MEN'S DOWNHILL WINNER.</headline>
<dateline>SESTRIERE, Italy 1997-02-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Profile of men's downhill winner on Saturday:</p>
<p>Name: Bruno Kernen</p>
<p>Age: 24</p>
<p>Nationality: Swiss</p>
<p>Previous World Cup wins: 2. Downhill - Veysonnaz I+II (96)</p>
<p>Other facts: Won world championship silver in the combined event on Thursday. Previous best world championship result was 16th in the downhill in 1993. Touted as next great Swiss all-rounder after the great Pirmin Zurbriggen but has struggled to live up to expectations.</p>
</text>
